            "content": "# Grill — usage reporting and reasoning effort on the WebPros LM Panel\n\nRaw evidence for a future OpenSpec proposal. Not a spec. Every claim below is\nfrom a command run on 2026-10-06 against `https://gateway.lmpanel.webpros.dev`\nwith Leo's panel key, or from reading a file named inline.\n\n## D1 — An OpenSpec proposal is not the required entry point here\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md: \"Bug fixes and chores may skip OpenSpec only when they do not\nchange a product contract.\" An engine defect that silently records no token\nusage for a whole provider type does not change a product contract. It changes\nwhether a declared contract holds on a wire that did not exist when the\ncontract was written.\n\n- Defect: usage is never reported for any `openai-completions` model.\n- Fix: one line, `includeUsage: true` at\n  `apps/api/src/models/openai-completions-model-client.ts:380`.\n- Existing spec (`run-usage-accounting`) already says what usage must record. It\n  is not satisfied on this wire. Fixing that satisfies it. No new requirement.\n\n## D2 — Effort control is reachable, and it is a discrete reasoning budget\n\n**Correction to the earlier claim in this conversation.** Reasoning on the panel\nis controlled through kit's `thinking.budget_tokens` on the Messages wire\n(`/v1/messages`), not through `reasoning_effort` on the Chat Completions wire\n(`/v1/chat/completions`). llame's `openai-completions` client only ever speaks\nthe latter.\n\nMeasured, `qwen3.8-27b`, `/v1/messages`, one hard puzzle prompt, n=3 per cell,\noutput tokens:\n\n| thinking shape | median output tokens | range |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| no key | 1147 | 1010-1187 |\n| `{type: disabled}` | 1018 | 978-1138 |\n| `{type: adaptive}` | 1424 | 1127-2775 |\n| `{type: enabled, budget_tokens: 1024}` | 1080 | 1005-1381 |\n| `{type: enabled, budget_tokens: 4096}` | 2752 | 2427-13910 |\n\nAnswer correctness was 3/3 in every cell, so the effect is on how much the model\nthinks, not on whether it is right.\n\nThe Messages endpoint reports usage by default on streaming and non-streaming,\nincluding `cache_creation_input_tokens` and `cache_read_input_tokens`. No\n`stream_options` needed on this wire.\n\n### What this means\n\n- The ready-made control on the panel is a **reasoning budget**, monotonic and\n  named (`budget_tokens`). It is not a `none`-to-`max` effort enum, and it does\n  not match llame's `reasoning.effortLevels` vocabulary.\n- llame's `anthropic-messages` client already composes\n  `thinking: { type: 'adaptive', display: 'summarized' }` when a model declares\n  `reasoning` (`apps/api/src/models/anthropic-model-client.ts:78`). If the panel\n  served Messages, declaring `reasoning` might already produce some thinking.\n  But the client's effort option is a closed Anthropic enum, and the adapter\n  may rewrite levels; the mapping from an effort level to a token budget is not\n  llame's to make silently.\n- **The reference implementation Leo already runs** is the `lmpanel-models`\n  Claude Code plugin (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/webpros/lmpanel-models/2.0.0`).\n  Its `src/gateway.mjs` routes `lmpanel/<id>` to the panel's `/v1/messages` with\n  the prefix stripped, the key swapped, assistant `thinking` blocks dropped, and\n  the identity sentence rewritten. Bodies verbatim otherwise. It is a router,\n  not a translator: it does not set effort either. So Claude Code's effort\n  reaching this model is not proven by that plugin.\n\n## D3 — The Chat Completions effort story is still unproven\n\nAn earlier probe in this conversation found `reasoning_effort` accepted but with\nno dose-response. A second pass at n=3 on the Messages wire found `output_config.effort`\naccepted with no monotonic effect. Neither is conclusive at that sample size.\nThe accurate statement is: **no effort or budget field on the Chat Completions\nwire was shown to change reasoning depth.** Budget-on-Messages was.\n\n## D4 — Three ways to reach the same capability, on different wires\n\n| wire | usage | thinking control | llame coverage |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Chat Completions `/v1/chat/completions` | only with `stream_options.include_usage` | `chat_template_kwargs.{thinking,enable_thinking}` works; `reasoning_effort` unproven | the wire `webpros-lmpanel` uses today |\n| Messages `/v1/messages` | reported by default, includes cache counters | `thinking.budget_tokens` works, dose-response shown | a second provider entry of type `anthropic-messages` could use it |\n| `count_tokens` | returns `{ \"input_tokens\": N }` | n/a | not used |\n\nThe Messages entry needs a `baseUrl` of `https://gateway.lmpanel.webpros.dev/v1`\nand the panel key in `key`; the client sends `x-api-key`, which the panel\naccepted in every probe above.\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. Does the panel's Messages endpoint accept llame's forced `anthropic-beta`\n   headers and its `thinking: { display: 'summarized'` } shape? Untested through\n   llame itself.\n2. Is a token budget the control llame wants to expose, given llame's effort\n   vocabulary is a provider-supplied string list and `reasoning.effortLevels`\n   is ordered? A budget is a number; presenting it as an effort level is a\n   mapping llame would be inventing.\n3. Does the Chat Completions wire have a thinking-budget equivalent\n   (`thinking_token_budget` was not tried)? If it does, the capability is\n   reachable without a second provider entry.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nRanked by leverage, not by completeness.\n\n1. Fix usage on `openai-completions` (`includeUsage: true`). It is a defect, it\n   is one line, and it restores a contract that already exists.\n2. Spike the remaining Chat Completions budget fields\n   (`thinking_token_budget`, `reasoning.max_tokens`) before designing an effort\n   surface. If one works, no second provider entry is needed.\n3. Only then decide between a budget surface and an effort surface. Do not\n   invent a `none`-to-`max` enum over an unproven field.\n",
