            "content": "# Grill — usage reporting and reasoning effort on the WebPros LM Panel\n\nEvidence for a future decision. Not a spec. Every claim is from a command run on\n2026-10-06 against `https://gateway.lmpanel.webpros.dev` with the panel key, or\nfrom a file named inline. Scratchpad artifacts:\n`effort3-ds.txt`, `effort3-qwen.txt`, `msgs-ds.txt`, `msgs-qwen.txt`,\n`proxy-log.jsonl`, `proxy.mjs`, `effort3.py`. Live config backed up at\n`live-config.backup.jsonc`; the working tree was restored and left clean.\n\n## Headline\n\n**Token usage is missing for one reason, and it is not the wire you use.**\nllame never asks the Chat Completions endpoint for usage. One boolean fixes it.\n\n**Effort is reachable as a discrete reasoning budget, not an effort enum.**\nThe knob is `thinking.budget_tokens` on the panel's Messages endpoint. It is\nreal and monotonic. It is not `reasoning_effort`, which does nothing anywhere.\n\n**The panel's Messages endpoint is half-built and cannot carry tools.** Every\nrequest llame sends with tools is rejected. That closes the \"just add a second\nprovider entry\" route.\n\n## The usage defect (one line, tracked source)\n\n`apps/api/src/models/openai-completions-model-client.ts:380` builds the provider\nwith `name`, `baseURL`, `apiKey`, `headers`, `fetch` — and no `includeUsage`.\n`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible@2.0.75` sends `stream_options: { include_usage: true }`\nonly when that flag is true (`dist/index.mjs:644`). The panel returns a usage\nchunk only when asked.\n\n- Raw proof: with the flag, one usage chunk arrives; without it, none.\n- SDK proof, driven through llame's own dependency: `includeUsage: false` gives\n  `{\"inputTokenDetails\":{},\"outputTokenDetails\":{}}`; `includeUsage: true` gives\n  32 input, 27 output, of which 24 reasoning, plus cache counters.\n- Live proof: the same prompt on `system:webpros-lmpanel:qwen3.8-27b` returns\n  `inputTokens: null, outputTokens: null, reasoningTokens: null`, even though the\n  model streamed 1524 characters of reasoning.\n\nThis is not LM-Panel-specific. It affects every `openai-completions` model,\nincluding `opencode-go`. `anthropic-messages` is unaffected: the panel reports\nusage by default there.\n\nAlso: `reasoning_tokens` arrives in `completion_tokens_details` and llame's\ntelemetry has a field for it, so it would populate too.\n\nCost stays `null` after the fix — the LM Panel models declare no pricing.\n\n## Reasoning effort — corrected\n\nEarlier in this conversation the claim was \"the gateway ignores reasoning\neffort\". That was measured on the wrong wire. The accurate version:\n\n| field | wire | effect |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reasoning_effort` (top level or in `chat_template_kwargs`) | Completions | no proven dose-response |\n| `thinking.budget_tokens` | Messages | real, monotonic |\n| `thinking.{thinking,enable_thinking: false}` | Completions | turns thinking off |\n| `output_config.effort` | Messages | accepted, no proven effect |\n\n`qwen3.8-27b`, Messages wire, n=3, one hard puzzle, output tokens:\n\n| shape | median | range |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| no key | 1431 | 749-1668 |\n| disabled | 1015 | 926-1788 |\n| budget 1024 | 850 | 753-1008 |\n| budget 4096 | 0 (timeout) | 0-13713 |\n| budget 8192 | 0 (timeout) | 0-0 |\n| effort low/high/max | 1093 / 887 / 1057 | scattered |\n\nAnswer correctness was 3/3 in every completed cell. Budget 4096 and above ran\npast a 280 s client timeout, so the effect is large, not subtle.\n\n`deepseek-v4-flash` on the Messages wire mostly timed out, so it is not a\nreliable route for that model.\n\n## The panel's Messages endpoint is unusable for llame now\n\nBisect of every shape llame's Messages client composes — `cache_control`,\n`system`, `thinking`, `tools`, `max_tokens`, beta headers — all accepted alone.\nThe failure is `tool_choice`:\n\n| request | result |\n| --- | --- |\n| tools, no `tool_choice` | OK |\n| tools, `{\"type\":\"auto\"}` (what llame sends) | rejected, 14 validation errors |\n| tools, `\"auto\"` string | 500, `'str' object has no attribute 'get'` |\n| tools, `{\"type\":\"tool\",\"name\":...}` | OK |\n\nThe 14 errors are all one field: the panel translates Messages to vLLM's\nResponses API and wants the OpenAI string form; llame sends Anthropic's object\nform. Rewriting to the string form gets past validation but hits the 500. There\nis no working value for `tool_choice` in the container form. This is a panel bug\nworth reporting, not something llame can configure around.\n\nCaptured with a local logging proxy (`proxy.mjs`) — the panel's own error text\nnames `vllm/entrypoints/serve/utils/api_utils.py ... create_responses`.\n\n## Claude Code on this model: settled\n\n`~/.claude/settings.json` sets `model: lmpanel/deepseek-v4-flash` and\n`modelSettings[\"lmpanel/deepseek-v4-flash\"].effortLevel: xhigh`. That session\ndoes not talk to the panel directly. It runs through the `lmpanel-models`\nplugin's loopback router (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/webpros/lmpanel-models/2.0.0/\nsrc/gateway.mjs`), which routes `lmpanel/<id>` to the panel and forwards bodies\nverbatim — it is a router, not a translator. It sets no effort field.\n\nSo Claude Code's own effort setting does not reach the panel model either. It\nmay shape Claude Code's client-side behavior, but no request field carries it to\nthe panel. The claim \"I can use effort with you in Claude Code\" is not supported\nby the request that actually goes out.\n\n## The dominant blocker is not effort or usage\n\nThe live site returns null usage on the tool-loop run because the model reached\nthe step cap without a final answer. Its reasoning text reports 42 entries in\n`/tmp` and lists files, yet the run's own answer claims it could not read the\ndirectory. Wrong tool results, a fabricated summary, or a prompt-injection\nartifact in `/tmp` — worth investigating before either spec.\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. Does the Completions wire carry a thinking-budget equivalent\n   (`thinking_token_budget`, `reasoning.max_tokens`)? Untried. If it does, the\n   budget capability is reachable with no second provider entry and no new wire.\n2. How would a token budget present as llame's `reasoning.effortLevels`, which\n   is an ordered list of provider strings? A budget is a number. Mapping one to\n   the other is a mapping llame would invent.\n3. Should the panel bug be reported to #lm-panel before llame depends on\n   Messages at all?\n\n## Priority\n\nOrdered by leverage.\n\n1. `includeUsage: true`. One line, restores an existing contract, unblocks cost,\n   usage display, and context accounting for a whole wire.\n2. Investigate the tool-loop failure above. It makes chat unusable and ranks\n   above any deliberate effort surface.\n3. Only then, effort: probe the Completions budget fields first. The Messages\n   route is closed by the panel bug.\n",
