ot something llame can configure around. I captured it with a local logging proxy.\n\n**Your Claude Code premise does not hold.** That session runs `lmpanel/deepseek-v4-flash` with `effortLevel: xhigh`, but it goes through the `lmpanel-models` plugin's loopback router, which forwards bodies to the panel verbatim and sets no effort field. So your effort setting does not reach the panel model either.\n\n**One thing outranks both.** On the live site the tool-loop run returned null usage because the model hit the step cap instead of answering. Its reasoning reports 42 entries in `/tmp` and starts listing files, yet its answer says it could not read the directory. That reads like bad tool results or an injection artifact in `/tmp`, and it makes chat unusable in a way that effort and usage do not.\n\nPriority: fix `includeUsage` first, then investigate that tool-loop failure, then decide the effort surface after probing whether the Completions wire has a budget field. The last two things are what I would put in OpenSpec; the first is a defect that satisfies the existing `run-usage-accounting` spec.\n\nNotes and raw evidence: `grill-notes.md` in the session scratchpad, alongside the proxy, spikes, and a config backup. I did not create an issue or a proposal.",
